# Day 39

## Experiment Title

Introduction to Continuous Integration using GitHub Actions


## Objective

To understand the basics of Continuous Integration and study the role of GitHub Actions in automating development workflows.


## Theory

Continuous Integration is a software development practice in which code changes are automatically tested and integrated into the main project repository. It helps developers identify errors early and improves software quality.

GitHub Actions is an automation tool provided by GitHub that allows users to create workflows for building, testing, and deploying applications automatically. Workflows are defined using YAML configuration files inside the repository.


## Requirements

GitHub Account

GitHub Repository

GitHub Actions

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Create or open a GitHub repository.

Access the GitHub Actions section inside the repository.

Study the workflow creation process in GitHub Actions.

Create a basic workflow configuration file.

Observe the execution process of the workflow after repository changes.


## Output

GitHub Actions workflow was created successfully.

The Continuous Integration process executed automatically after repository updates.

Workflow execution details were displayed successfully in GitHub Actions.


## Result

Successfully understood the basics of Continuous Integration using GitHub Actions.
